{\b\fs24 Hopp terms of use}\par
These terms are short on purpose. By installing and using Hopp you agree to them.\par
{\b Hopp is in beta}\par
Hopp works every day, but it is still young. Expect bugs and changes. It is free and comes "as is", without any promise that it will always work or always be available. Don't rely on it for anything where a failure could cause harm, such as emergencies.\par
{\b Your Hopp ID}\par
Your account is a key kept on your computer, protected by your password. Your 24-word recovery phrase is the only way back into your account if you lose your password or your computer. Keep it somewhere safe and never share it: anyone who has it can take over your account, and nobody, including Hopp, can recover an account without it.\par
{\b Be decent}\par
Don't use Hopp to break the law, to harass, threaten or spam people, to share content that exploits children, or to spread malware or scams. Server owners and moderators can remove people from their servers. Accounts and servers that break these rules can be removed from Hopp Cloud.\par
{\b Your content}\par
What you write, say and share is yours, and you are responsible for it. Voice, calls, screen sharing and files go straight between you and the people you talk to. Direct messages are end-to-end encrypted. Messages in servers on Hopp Cloud are kept so the server can show its history.\par
{\b Privacy}\par
Hopp doesn't sell your data, show ads or track you. How your information is handled is explained at hopp-cloud.hoppchat.workers.dev/privacy.\par
{\b Limits and changes}\par
Hopp Cloud has limits to stay free, listed in the app and on the website. These terms may change as Hopp grows; when they do, the app will say so. If you don't agree with a change, you can stop using Hopp and uninstall it at any time.\par
{\b Liability}\par
As far as the law allows, Hopp is not liable for lost data, lost messages or other damage from using it.\par
